{"reply": "Great, so you are using Ubuntu! To update your packages on Ubuntu, you should use the following command in your terminal: `sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade`

First, `sudo apt update` will refresh the package lists from the repositories. Then, `sudo apt upgrade` will upgrade all packages that have new versions available.

It is recommended to run these commands as root, so make sure you are using `sudo` before each command to execute them with administrator privileges.", "steps": [{"type": "info", "title": "Step 1", "description": "Refresh package lists", "command": "sudo apt update"}], "has_more_steps": true}
